`canonical_json` is UTF-8, sorted keys, compact separators, `allow_nan=False`; `sha256_hex` hashes those bytes. `validate_roi` is the shared box gate. `validate_inventory(inv, *, expected_reference_photo_id, expected_sha256=None)` returns `sha256`, `reference_photo_id`, `attribute_ids`, `inventory`. `validate_response(payload, ids, *, expected_inventory_sha256)` returns a deep copy of the same shape, so T2d gets `results` as a list. Both pins are required keywords, so a forgotten pin fails closed. One choice to confirm: `candidate_roi` is always a box; the spec allows null only for `reference_roi` under `NOT_VISIBLE_IN_REFERENCE`.

